  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (differences from reference value weighted by probability) is mathematically equivalent to the expected value in this case, since the reference value is zero. The individual considered exactly this information—expected gain—by calculating the mean outcomes. Furthermore, the decision rule used by the individual (choosing the lottery with the higher expected gain) aligns with the rule of the decision reason (choosing the lottery with the more favorable mean difference). Although the individual does not mention the reference value or frame the calculation in terms of differences, the underlying computation and decision rule are identical. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used the reasoning process described by the decision reason, even if not articulated in the same terms.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
}

{
